Subject: [PATCH KW2/3] key-web: exfiltration-proof CSP, Connection-Allowlist
 and KeyWebNavigationThrottle

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
Copyright 2026 The Key-Origin Web Authors
Target: Chromium 160.0.8176.0 (apply after KW1: patch -p1 -d src < this.patch)

Tier 0 egress lockdown for key-web:// documents (Spec §2.2-§2.8).

L1 CSP (components/webapps/key_web/policy/header_policy.*)
  Enforced on every key-web response, added next to the app's own policy so
  an app can only tighten it:
    default-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'self' data: blob:;
    form-action 'none'
  plus script/style/media/font/worker/frame/manifest/object/base-uri/
  frame-ancestors/trusted-types hardening, none of which adds a network
  source. There is NO `navigate-to`: Chromium 160 does not implement it
  (absent from network::mojom::CSPDirectiveName), and an ignored directive
  would give false assurance.

L2 Connection-Allowlist
  `(response-origin);redirects=block;webrtc=block`. response-origin is the
  non-network key-web origin, so the network service refuses ResolveHost,
  PreconnectSockets, Prefetch, WebTransport and WebRTC binders for the
  document. This is the load-bearing control for <link rel=preconnect>,
  which bypasses CSP and X-DNS-Prefetch-Control in M160.

L3 Navigation Gate (chrome/browser/key_web/key_web_navigation_throttle.*)
  KeyWebNavigationThrottle runs on WillStartRequest and WillRedirectRequest
  for navigations whose initiator is a key-web origin:
    same origin / about:blank / about:srcdoc / data:  -> PROCEED
    prerender, speculation rules                      -> CANCEL
    cross-origin subframe (ambient egress)            -> BLOCK_REQUEST
    cross-origin top level without user gesture       -> BLOCK_REQUEST
    cross-origin top level with user gesture          -> CANCEL, then a
      browser-owned tab-modal prompt shows the FULL URL (Open / Copy /
      Cancel). Open is a browser-initiated new foreground tab: no opener,
      no referrer, no key-web initiator.
  ChromeContentBrowserClient::CanCreateWindow() applies the same gate to
  window.open() and target=_blank before any other feature handles them.

L5 Header sanitizer
  App-supplied Report-To, Reporting-Endpoints, NEL, *-Report-Only,
  Connection-Allowlist*, Allow-Connection-Allowlist-From, Link, Refresh,
  Speculation-Rules, Set-Cookie, Alt-Svc, ... are stripped, and report-uri /
  report-to directives are removed from app CSP headers.

DNS prefetch / preconnect hints
  * X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off is injected (irreversible per document).
  * OverrideWebPreferences{,AfterNavigation}() clear
    WebPreferences::dns_prefetching_enabled while the main frame is key-web.
  * NetworkHintsHandlerImpl::{PrefetchDNS,Preconnect} drop hints from any
    frame that is, or is nested in, a key-web document before they reach
    the PreconnectManager.

KW3 calls key_web::SetRequiredHeadersForKeyWeb() from the loader factory.

Tests: unit_tests --gtest_filter='KeyWebNavigationPolicyTest.*:KeyWebHeaderPolicyTest.*'

